<title>GERMANY: Hannover Re 1996 premiums rose 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Hannover Re 1996 premiums rose 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group gross premiums		 6,200  up 3 pct</p>
<p>Capital investments (unconsolidated) 13,800 up 15 pct</p>
<p>								  (approx)</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is Hannover Rueckversicherungs AG (Hanover Re), the world's fifth largest reinsurance group. The company also said in an interim report it expected its pre-tax profits to achieve a double digit rise to around 130 million marks from 116 million marks. It said it expected earnings from capital investments to rise more than 20 percent to 750 million marks, although underwriting earnings would worsen because of expansion costs.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
